Z||000000||FieroGTGirl||05-06-2000||04:30 PM||||What is the first thing to check when your windshield wiper fluid doesn't work(yes guys...I have checked if there was fluid in the reservoir) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||05-06-2000||04:36 PM||||Check the little hoses, the do get pluged some times. Any gunk in the bottle?||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||05-06-2000||04:43 PM|||| stuff to try. can you hear the washer pump working with some one holding the switch? no puddles from a broken hose? got a meter to see if you have voltage to pump when switched on? maybe switch feels different (broken)? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||05-06-2000||04:44 PM||||Is it completely dead, or does it just work very poorly?  Do you have a shop manual yet?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroGTGirl||05-06-2000||05:57 PM||||Thanks for the advice I will check into it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||05-06-2000||08:25 PM||||100 bucks says it's the pump. Look at the tank and you will see a black tubular thing sticking out of it with hoses attatched to it. This just twists out. If you don't have/can't find another one I have one I know works I will give you.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||05-06-2000||10:40 PM||||Mine went dead on my 84 fiero, so i just guessed thats what was wrong with it.  I went to the junkyard and pulled one from a fiero, there is no screws holding it.  Payed a couple of bucks and mine is back to normal.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Linx||05-07-2000||09:44 PM||||Holy cow- you went to a junk yard for a washer motor?  These are srandard GM issue...Autozone sells 'em for $8.  And thyere held in by a grommet. 15 second repair...everything on this car should be that easy...like the dew wipes for instance.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
