Z||000009||GT-maniac||05-08-2000||11:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by phillip:<BR><B> stuff to try. can you hear the washer pump working with some one holding the switch? no puddles from a broken hose? got a meter to see if you have voltage to pump when switched on? maybe switch feels different (broken)? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have this problem too, my washer doesn't seem to work at all. When I press the switch I can't hear anything. I replaced the pump but I think the problem may be a lack of power. The under hood light doesn't work either, are they on the same circuit ? Is their something else on the same cicuit ?.<BR>My car has lots of electrical problems. The power trunk release, oil pressure gauge, license plate lights and trunk lights all don't work either. A friend gave me a multimeter but how do I use it to test for power ? or if the wiring is broken ? <BR>||||reg||9
